![context sweep](../results/fig_context.png)

The designs come nearer to each other as context increases. S is {{ x(I.context.s_over_a.at_8k) }} faster than A at 8K and
{{ x(I.context.s_over_a.at_1m) }} at 1M tokens. At 1M tokens a step reads
{{ gb(I.context.kv[-1].kv_full_bytes + I.context.kv[-1].kv_draft_bytes, 0) }} of KV cache
({{ pct(I.context.kv[-1].kv_share_of_bytes) }} of all bytes that a GPU step moves). That traffic is the
same on every platform. A chip with its weights on-die still needs fast KV memory.

The KV cache can be in LPDDR instead of HBM. The pool is then {{ n(I.kv_memory.lpddr_pool_bytes_per_s / 1e12, 2) }} TB/s against
{{ n(I.kv_memory.hbm_pool_bytes_per_s / 1e12, 0) }} TB/s (pool size is an assumption). With LPDDR, S falls behind A
above about {{ n(I.kv_memory.crossover_context_vs_a, -3) }} tokens of context. It falls behind the GPUs above
about {{ n(I.kv_memory.crossover_context_vs_g0, -3) }}.

The published GPU figures also decrease with context. The vLLM throughput per GPU decreases from about
{{ n(M.vllm_gb200_tp8_32k.value) }} at 32K to about {{ n(M.vllm_gb200_tp8_256k.value) }} at 256K
(measured; vllm-blog).

