| tokens/J, batch 1 | {{ n(s.batch1.tokens_per_joule, 2) }} | {{ n(f.batch1.tokens_per_joule, 2) }} | {{ x(s.batch1.tokens_per_joule / f.batch1.tokens_per_joule, 2) }} |
| tokens/J, best point | {{ n(s.best_energy.tokens_per_joule, 2) }} | {{ n(f.best_energy.tokens_per_joule, 2) }} | {{ x(s.best_energy.tokens_per_joule / f.best_energy.tokens_per_joule, 2) }} |
| $/M tokens, best point | {{ usd(s.best_cost.usd_per_mtok, 3) }} | {{ usd(f.best_cost.usd_per_mtok, 3) }} | {{ x(s.best_cost.usd_per_mtok / f.best_cost.usd_per_mtok, 2) }} |
| distinct die designs | {{ I.designs.s.cost.distinct_die_designs }} | {{ I.designs.f.cost.distinct_die_designs }} | |
| masks to change for a new model version | none: load new weights | {{ usd(I.designs.f.cost.unique_mask_usd / 1e6, 1) }}M of unique mask layers | |

Reloadability costs {{ x(I.designs.s_over_f.dies, 1) }} the silicon and {{ x(s.best_cost.usd_per_mtok / f.best_cost.usd_per_mtok, 1) }} in decode cost per token.
At a busy operating point it costs {{ x(f.best_energy.tokens_per_joule / s.best_energy.tokens_per_joule, 2) }} in tokens per joule.

**The speed difference in the table is not a cost of reloadability.** S takes its time per weight
operation from a published wafer-scale SRAM machine. F takes its time from a published fixed-weight chip. The
synthesized fixed-weight datapath closes timing at the same clock as the reloadable datapath (its best period
is slightly slower). Thus, on the clock and latency of S, F is not faster. The {{ x(f.batch1.tok_s_user / s.batch1.tok_s_user, 1) }} is a difference
between the machines of two vendors.

Reloadability gives one die design instead of {{ I.designs.f.cost.distinct_die_designs }}. To get a new model
version, a fine-tune or a different model of the same family, you load weights and do not tape out.
The fixed design here also assumes that a published single-die result at 8B parameters (measured;
taalas-hc1) applies to a model 74x larger on {{ I.designs.f.area.dies }} dies. The only public figure
for a model of this class on that approach is the simulation of the vendor, not a measurement.
[07](07_silicon.md) gives the synthesized datapath that is the source of the area and energy ratio.

