## 14 · Where purpose-built silicon does not win

- **Cost at ordinary interactive speed**: at {{ n(I.headline.sla_tok_s_user) }} tok/s per user the decode cost gain of S is {{ x(RS.cost_best) }}
  in the central case. It is {{ x(MC.cost_best.median, 2) }} at the median. With a seller's margin of 50% it is {{ x(I.margin.rows[-1].cost_gain, 2) }} (section 19).
- **Prefill**: at its best concurrency S prefills at {{ x(I.prefill.s_over_g0_cost, 2) }} the GPUs' cost per token, and the HBM chip at
  {{ x(I.prefill.a_over_g0_cost, 1) }} (section 6).
- **Low demand**: below about {{ n(I.demand.breakeven_tokens_per_day.s / 1e12, 1) }} trillion tokens a day S does not recover its design cost (section 18).
- **Small models**: the speed gain decreases to {{ x(I.ladder.rung_8b.gain.S.speed_batch1) }} at about 8B, and the cost gain falls below 1 (section 9).
- **Long context**: the lead over an HBM chip decreases from {{ x(I.context.s_over_a.at_8k) }} to {{ x(I.context.s_over_a.at_1m) }}. With cheap KV
  memory, S falls behind the HBM chip above about {{ n(I.kv_memory.crossover_context_vs_a, -3) }} tokens (section 5).
- **A single request**: S gets {{ x(I.power_management.managed.over_g0_best_batch, 2) }} of the tokens per joule of a busy GPU cluster even with power
  management, and {{ x(I.power_management.unmanaged.over_g0_best_batch, 2) }} without it (section 8).
- **Software**: {{ x(RG.speed_batch1) }} of the batch-1 speed gain is available on the GPUs that are already installed (section 2).
- **All that this study did not model**: vision input, reasoning-length variation, failures, and the
  years that are necessary to build a chip ([05](05_limitations.md)).

